                <pb facs="0591" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.48B/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Woods</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Iwaki</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                        1923</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 10:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Communications have just been opened up with Yokohama. The situation there is
                    exceedingly serious and some Americans are reported to have lost their lives.
                    The casualties in Tokio are estimated at 10,000. I believe all Americans in
                    Tokio are safe. The food situation is acute. Send supply from Philippines at
                    once as already requested. The fire-proof vault of the Embassy was not
                    fire-proof and all Embassy records are burned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Woods</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
